<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>08 · CONCLUSIONS</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Four claims we can defend — with their strength attached
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', marginTop: 8 }}>
        {[
            ['01', 'Chain-aware arms mostly do not pay', '12 of 19 cells sit below zero; median −0.010 across cells (−0.098 across readings). Deepest cell is dielectric loss (−1.479, 279 rows); most stable is op_tm × A3 (−0.859, 75 readings) — two different cells.'],
            ['02', 'Stratification is refuted, but not cleanly tested', 'ρ = +0.000 / +0.239. At matched n, tier 1 stays below tier 2 (−0.033 / −0.087, intervals excluding zero) — so the break is inside tier 3, not the sample-size confound.'],
            ['03', 'On the ratio ruler it has not halved; on the absolute one it has', 'Λ ratio 0.650 and κ = −0.086 [−0.105, −0.067]: not halved, and the first tenfold step even rises (+0.073/dex). The absolute ruler halves the same curve, to 0.0066 — the same order as the per-task floor (0.0046). They disagree because the denominator collapses 0.135 → 0.034.'],
            ['04', 'Information versus architecture stays unanswerable', 'A5 cannot be constructed from the data, so its zero count is a boundary, not a debt. The substitute is a per-task floor: median 0.0046, cleared by 5 of 8 tasks.'],
        ].map(([num, head, body], i) => (
            <Box key={num} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 24, paddingTop: 7, paddingBottom: 7, borderTop: i === 0 ? '0px solid #1D2A40' : '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF', width: 44, lineHeight: 1.2 }}>{num}</Text>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', flex: 1 }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.25 }}>{head}</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 3, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>{body}</Text>
                </Box>
            </Box>
        ))}
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', padding: '12px 22px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '3px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 27, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.25 }}>
            A richer encoding of the repeat unit does not recover it — and the chain itself stayed untestable here.
        </Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 6, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
            Its weight is bounded by two undecidable points, one arm we could not build, and one measurement protocol (6 of 6 tasks are experimental labels).
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 10 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>14 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
